<!-- [XPLAT] migrated from net48/WinForms — see MIGRATION_DOCS/TRANSITION_MAP.md -->
<!--
    [XPLAT] AgOpenGPS (GPS program) — Roll Correction Chart dialog (Avalonia view).

    1:1 visual parity reimplementation of the WinForms `Forms/Settings/FormCorrection`
    (source: FormCorrection.cs + FormCorrection.Designer.cs) — the live antenna pole-sway /
    roll diagnostics screen. It plots three rolling traces (roll correction distance, corrected
    easting, uncorrected easting) over a black chart and shows their live numeric readouts along
    the bottom. Per AAP §0.3.3 this is a faithful re-platform of the current Windows Forms look,
    never a redesign: every size, font and colour below is taken verbatim from
    FormCorrection.Designer.cs.

    KEY MIGRATION CHANGE (DataVisualization chart replaced by custom Avalonia drawing):
      The WinForms `rollChart` was a Windows-only DataVisualization charting control that was dropped
      from AgOpenGPS.csproj during the migration. It is reimplemented here as a lightweight custom
      Avalonia control (`local:RollChart`) that buffers the last 50 samples per series and paints
      step-line polylines in its Render(DrawingContext) — no new NuGet dependency, and no legacy
      Windows-only UI or GL-host types are referenced (Avalonia markup only).

    WINDOW SHELL — mirrors FormCorrection.Designer.cs:
      Form.Text "Roll Correction Chart" -> Title
      ClientSize 809 x 424              -> Width / Height (SystemDecorations="None" => client == window)
      FormBorderStyle.None (implied)    -> SystemDecorations="None"
      (fixed size, not resizable)       -> CanResize="False"
      ShowInTaskbar = false             -> ShowInTaskbar="False"
      StartPosition.CenterParent        -> WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner" (shown over FormGPS)
      Window chrome                      -> Background="{DynamicResource AogFrameBrush}" (per AAP file
                                            spec; uses the App.axaml day/night frame brush so the thin
                                            top strip and the bottom readout band pick up the live theme,
                                            while the dominant chart surface stays black for parity).

    THEME / COLOUR NOTE:
      The chart surface and the per-series / readout colours are hard-coded (Black background;
      Red / Lime / Cyan traces; Chartreuse / LightSalmon labels) straight from the WinForms source
      because this is a fixed instrumentation palette, not themed chrome — identical to how the
      original FormCorrection ignored the day/night skin for its plot. Only the Window background
      uses the {DynamicResource AogFrameBrush} theme brush, per this file's AAP spec.

    LAYOUT MODEL:
      The WinForms designer positioned every control absolutely (Location/Size) with the chart
      behind and the labels / buttons painted on top. That overlapping, fixed pixel layout is
      reproduced faithfully with a root Canvas using Canvas.Left / Canvas.Top equal to the original
      designer coordinates; declaration order reproduces the original z-order (chart first/behind,
      then the buttons and labels on top). The window is fixed-size (CanResize="False"), so absolute
      positioning is exact and needs no reflow.

    FONT SIZES:
      WinForms Font sizes are in points; Avalonia FontSize is in device-independent pixels, so each
      value is converted px = pt * 96 / 72: readouts Tahoma 18pt -> 24; descriptive labels Tahoma
      14.25pt -> 19; buttons Microsoft Sans Serif 12pt -> 16.

    WIRING CONTRACT — this view is IMPERATIVE (code-behind), NOT MVVM:
      There is intentionally NO x:DataType, NO DataContext and NO {Binding}; the partner code-behind
      FormCorrectionView.axaml.cs drives everything by addressing the named controls directly, exactly
      like the sibling FormYesView / FormInputDialogView. The x:Name values below are the contract and
      MUST NOT change. The partner code-behind (partial class
      AgOpenGPS.Views.Settings.FormCorrectionView : Window) is expected to:
        * Declare a constructor that calls InitializeComponent().
        * Own these named controls: rollChart, lblCorrectionDistance, lblEast, lblOst, lblRollDegrees,
          lblEastOnGraph, btnScroll, btnPoleOrMoving.
        * On a timer (interval = 1000 / gpsHz, as in FormCorrection.cs) recompute the readouts and,
          while scrolling is enabled, push one sample (roll, easting, uncorrected easting; each x20,
          matching DrawChart) into rollChart, which keeps the most recent 50 per series.
        * Provide the two Click handlers referenced below:
            btnScroll_Click_1(object sender, RoutedEventArgs e)  -> toggles freeze/scroll (FormCorrection
              isScroll = !isScroll); the original WinForms handler name is preserved.
            btnPoleOrMoving_Click(object sender, RoutedEventArgs e) -> toggles pole/moving (isPole) and
              flips btnPoleOrMoving.Content between "Pole" and "Moving". (WinForms used Button.Text;
              the Avalonia equivalent is Button.Content, which is why btnPoleOrMoving below carries a
              plain string Content the handler can reassign.)

    CUSTOM CHART CONTROL CONTRACT — `local:RollChart`:
      `local` is this view's own namespace (AgOpenGPS.Views.Settings). RollChart is a custom plotting
      control implemented in the C# layer as:
            public class RollChart : Avalonia.Controls.Control   // parameterless ctor
      and is expected to:
        * Hold three rolling sample buffers, each capped at the most recent 50 points, named to match
          the WinForms series: "Ro" (roll / correction distance), "Ze" (corrected easting) and
          "Oe" (uncorrected easting).
        * Use the exact per-series colours copied from FormCorrection.Designer.cs:
          "Ro" = Red (border width 2), "Ze" = Lime, "Oe" = Cyan.
        * Override Render(DrawingContext) to auto-scale the buffered samples to the control bounds and
          stroke each series as a StepLine polyline (matching SeriesChartType.StepLine), over the black
          background supplied by its host Border below; call InvalidateVisual() when samples change.
      The control needs no XAML-set properties here (Avalonia's Control base has no Background of its
      own — the surrounding Border provides the black backdrop), so only x:Name is set on it.
-->
<Window xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        xmlns:gStr="clr-namespace:AgOpenGPS.Core.Translations;assembly=AgOpenGPS.Core"
        xmlns:local="clr-namespace:AgOpenGPS.Views.Settings"
        x:Class="AgOpenGPS.Views.Settings.FormCorrectionView"
        Title="Roll Correction Chart"
        Width="809"
        Height="424"
        Background="{DynamicResource AogFrameBrush}"
        SystemDecorations="None"
        CanResize="False"
        ShowInTaskbar="False"
        WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner"
        FontFamily="Tahoma">

    <!--
        btnScroll / btnPoleOrMoving styling. WinForms: FlatStyle.Flat with FlatAppearance.BorderColor
        = Silver, BackColor = Transparent, ForeColor = Lime, Microsoft Sans Serif 12pt Bold. Reproduced
        as a `flat` Button class: a transparent, silver-outlined, lime-text button. The :pointerover and
        :pressed setters target the Fluent template's content presenter so the theme's hover / pressed
        fill never paints over the flat transparent face (same technique as Keypad / FormYesView),
        keeping the silver border and lime text in every interaction state.
    -->
    <Window.Styles>
        <Style Selector="Button.flat">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Silver" />
            <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="1" />
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="Lime" />
            <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="Microsoft Sans Serif" />
            <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="16" />
            <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="Bold" />
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="2" />
            <Setter Property="HorizontalContentAlignment" Value="Center" />
            <Setter Property="VerticalContentAlignment" Value="Center" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Button.flat:pointerover /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Silver" />
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="Lime" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Button.flat:pressed /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Silver" />
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="Lime" />
        </Style>
    </Window.Styles>

    <!--
        Root Canvas reproduces the WinForms absolute layout (client 809 x 424). Children are declared
        bottom-to-top to match the original control z-order: the chart paints first (behind), then the
        command buttons and the readout / descriptive labels paint on top.
    -->
    <Canvas>

        <!-- rollChart host. WinForms Chart: Location (-30,9) Size 830 x 372, BackColor Black. The
             negative left / 830 width only pushed the auto-generated axis labels off the left edge so
             the plot filled the form width; the custom RollChart manages its own rendering, so the
             surface is normalised to the visible region (Left 0, Width 809, Top 9, Height 372). The
             Border supplies the black backdrop and clips the traces to the plot rectangle; RollChart
             fills it. AutomationProperties.Name gives the non-textual plot an accessible label. -->
        <Border Canvas.Left="0"
                Canvas.Top="9"
                Width="809"
                Height="372"
                Background="Black"
                ClipToBounds="True"
                AutomationProperties.Name="Roll correction chart">
            <local:RollChart x:Name="rollChart" />
        </Border>

        <!-- btnScroll — WinForms Location (12,12) Size 92 x 60, Text "Scroll On Off". Freezes / resumes
             the trace (FormCorrection isScroll). The label wraps across lines inside the narrow button,
             as it did in WinForms. Click -> code-behind btnScroll_Click_1. -->
        <Button x:Name="btnScroll" AutomationProperties.Name="Scroll On Off"
                Classes="flat"
                Canvas.Left="12"
                Canvas.Top="12"
                Width="92"
                Height="60"
                Click="btnScroll_Click_1">
            <TextBlock Text="Scroll On Off"
                       TextWrapping="Wrap"
                       TextAlignment="Center" />
        </Button>

        <!-- btnPoleOrMoving — WinForms Location (14,301) Size 92 x 60, Text "Pole". Toggles pole vs
             moving correction (FormCorrection isPole); the code-behind reassigns Content to "Moving" /
             "Pole". Content is a plain string (not a TextBlock) so that reassignment stays as simple as
             the original Button.Text swap. Click -> code-behind btnPoleOrMoving_Click. -->
        <Button x:Name="btnPoleOrMoving"
                Classes="flat"
                Canvas.Left="14"
                Canvas.Top="301"
                Width="92"
                Height="60"
                Content="Pole"
                Click="btnPoleOrMoving_Click" />

        <!-- lblEastOnGraph — WinForms Location (705,4) Size 105 x 29, Lime 18pt Bold, MiddleRight,
             BackColor black. Live integer easting overlay at the top-right of the plot. -->
        <Border Canvas.Left="705"
                Canvas.Top="4"
                Width="105"
                Height="29"
                Background="Black">
            <TextBlock x:Name="lblEastOnGraph"
                       Text="0"
                       Foreground="Lime"
                       FontFamily="Tahoma"
                       FontSize="24"
                       FontWeight="Bold"
                       TextAlignment="Right"
                       VerticalAlignment="Center" />
        </Border>

        <!-- ===================== Bottom readout band (left -> right) ===================== -->
        <!-- Each pairing is a black chip (Border, reproducing the WinForms label BackColor) carrying a
             vertically-centred coloured TextBlock. Descriptive captions are right-aligned and wrap to
             two lines (matching the WinForms multi-line labels); the live readouts are left-aligned. -->

        <!-- label3 "Antenna" — WinForms (22,387) 84 x 29, Cyan 14.25pt, MiddleRight. -->
        <Border Canvas.Left="22" Canvas.Top="387" Width="84" Height="29" Background="Black">
            <TextBlock Text="Antenna"
                       Foreground="Cyan"
                       FontFamily="Tahoma"
                       FontSize="19"
                       TextAlignment="Right"
                       TextWrapping="Wrap"
                       VerticalAlignment="Center" />
        </Border>

        <!-- lblOst — WinForms (102,387) 85 x 29, Cyan 18pt Bold, MiddleLeft. Uncorrected easting. -->
        <Border Canvas.Left="102" Canvas.Top="387" Width="85" Height="29" Background="Black">
            <TextBlock x:Name="lblOst"
                       Text="0.00"
                       Foreground="Cyan"
                       FontFamily="Tahoma"
                       FontSize="24"
                       FontWeight="Bold"
                       Padding="3,0,0,0"
                       TextAlignment="Left"
                       VerticalAlignment="Center" />
        </Border>

        <!-- label5 "Corrected Easting" — WinForms (214,372) 98 x 55, Chartreuse 14.25pt, MiddleRight. -->
        <Border Canvas.Left="214" Canvas.Top="372" Width="98" Height="55" Background="Black">
            <TextBlock Text="Corrected Easting"
                       Foreground="Chartreuse"
                       FontFamily="Tahoma"
                       FontSize="19"
                       TextAlignment="Right"
                       TextWrapping="Wrap"
                       VerticalAlignment="Center" />
        </Border>

        <!-- lblEast — WinForms (309,386) 85 x 29, Lime 18pt Bold, MiddleLeft. Corrected easting. -->
        <Border Canvas.Left="309" Canvas.Top="386" Width="85" Height="29" Background="Black">
            <TextBlock x:Name="lblEast"
                       Text="0.00"
                       Foreground="Lime"
                       FontFamily="Tahoma"
                       FontSize="24"
                       FontWeight="Bold"
                       Padding="3,0,0,0"
                       TextAlignment="Left"
                       VerticalAlignment="Center" />
        </Border>

        <!-- label1 "Correction Distance" — WinForms (438,375) 97 x 46, Red 14.25pt, MiddleRight. -->
        <Border Canvas.Left="438" Canvas.Top="375" Width="97" Height="46" Background="Black">
            <TextBlock Text="Correction Distance"
                       Foreground="Red"
                       FontFamily="Tahoma"
                       FontSize="19"
                       TextAlignment="Right"
                       TextWrapping="Wrap"
                       VerticalAlignment="Center" />
        </Border>

        <!-- lblCorrectionDistance — WinForms (533,386) 85 x 29, Red 18pt Bold, MiddleLeft. -->
        <Border Canvas.Left="533" Canvas.Top="386" Width="85" Height="29" Background="Black">
            <TextBlock x:Name="lblCorrectionDistance"
                       Text="0.00"
                       Foreground="Red"
                       FontFamily="Tahoma"
                       FontSize="24"
                       FontWeight="Bold"
                       Padding="3,0,0,0"
                       TextAlignment="Left"
                       VerticalAlignment="Center" />
        </Border>

        <!-- label6 "Roll Degrees" — WinForms (642,376) 85 x 47, LightSalmon 14.25pt, MiddleRight. -->
        <Border Canvas.Left="642" Canvas.Top="376" Width="85" Height="47" Background="Black">
            <TextBlock Text="Roll Degrees"
                       Foreground="LightSalmon"
                       FontFamily="Tahoma"
                       FontSize="19"
                       TextAlignment="Right"
                       TextWrapping="Wrap"
                       VerticalAlignment="Center" />
        </Border>

        <!-- lblRollDegrees — WinForms (725,384) 85 x 29, LightSalmon 18pt Bold, MiddleLeft. -->
        <Border Canvas.Left="725" Canvas.Top="384" Width="85" Height="29" Background="Black">
            <TextBlock x:Name="lblRollDegrees"
                       Text="0.0"
                       Foreground="LightSalmon"
                       FontFamily="Tahoma"
                       FontSize="24"
                       FontWeight="Bold"
                       Padding="3,0,0,0"
                       TextAlignment="Left"
                       VerticalAlignment="Center" />
        </Border>

    </Canvas>
</Window>
